# Prettier formats this project's own code and configs — nothing else.
#
# `scripts/ci.sh fast` runs `prettier --check .`, so anything NOT ignored here is
# a gate failure. Two kinds of file must stay out:
#
#   1. Plugin-owned files. `/workflow-update` replaces them from the plugin, so
#      formatting them fixes the gate exactly once and breaks it again at the
#      next update. `.claude/**`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` and
#      `docs/dev/code-style.md` are all in this category.
#   2. Prose. Reformatting markdown reflows tables and wraps paragraphs on every
#      edit, producing diff noise that hides the actual change. Prettier is a
#      code formatter here, not a prose formatter.
#
# Add project-owned code paths back by deleting a line, never by reformatting a
# plugin-owned file.

# --- plugin-owned (replaced on every /workflow-update) ---
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
docs/dev/code-style.md

# --- prose ---
*.md
docs/

# --- CI config: GitHub Actions expression syntax, and these are template-derived ---
.github/

# --- generated / vendored ---
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
node_modules/
src/version.ts
package-lock.json
*.min.*
